fact WorkItem(id: "WI-380", description: some(value: "Stdlib: migrate Stream/Iterable/Collection threading signatures to EXPLICIT operation type parameters (042) + WRITTEN effect rows (WI-375). The concrete stdlib consumer of WI-379 (bidirectional inference) that makes the threading SOUND in the type rather than via implicit sort-parameter sharing (dropped 2026-06-04, see docs/design/type-parameter-scoping.md). REWRITE the bare/implicit signatures: iterator(l: List) -> Stream  =>  iterator[Elem](l: List[T=Elem]) -> Stream[T=Elem, E={}] (element via [Elem]; observation effect WRITTEN E={} since List is pure -- WI-375 surface, DELIVERED); collect(s: Stream) -> List[T] effects E  =>  collect[Elem,Eff](s: Stream[T=Elem,E=Eff]) -> List[T=Elem] effects Eff; same for splitFirst (tail B = Stream[T=Elem,E=Eff], head A=Elem), takeN, head, tail, isEmpty. An effectful carrier writes E={Modify[c]} (correctly rejected in a pure consumer); abstract carriers stay polymorphic (the spec's [Elem,Eff] thread). This + WI-379 closes the WI-368 ?_ leak (length(collect(List.iterator(xs))) typechecks pure AND the element threads to List[Int]) and resolves the concrete/abstract split. RELATION: WI-379 (the typer inference this relies on -- args-before-expected + cross-sort binding); WI-368 (the effect-grounding acceptance, achieved by this rewrite + WI-379); WI-376 (projection s.T/s.Sort is the FLUENT alternative surface to [Elem,Eff] -- either threads; this WI uses 042 explicit, projection optional later); WI-375/WI-307 (written rows, delivered). ACCEPTANCE: stdlib loads green; length(collect(List.iterator(xs))) pure with element List[Int]; an abstract Iterable walk stays effect-polymorphic; wi357/wi362/wi365/wi368 + full anthill-core green. Authoritative sequence: docs/design/expansion-during-unification.md sec.8. Rust/stdlib (signatures); typer behind it is WI-379."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-379", "WI-392", "WI-393"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-05T14:36:56Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-380", author: "user", content: "BLOCKED on the new prerequisite WI (written effect rows in fact-head positions + cross-sort provider-view E admissibility). Implementing WI-380 surfaced that 'iterator[Elem](l: List[T=Elem]) -> Stream[T=Elem, E={}] = l' needs (a) 'fact Stream[T=T, E={}]' to LOAD (fact-head {} loader gap) and (b) the cross-sort subtype check to thread that E from the provider fact (parameterized_compatible_view gap). The ELEMENT half works ('iterator -> Stream[T=Elem]' threads List[Int] via collect); the EFFECT half (WI-368 pure: length(collect(List.iterator(xs)))) needs the prerequisite. Sequence the prerequisite BEFORE WI-380; resume the producer rewrites (write E={}) once it lands. wi368_iterator_threading_test holds the acceptance (currently #[ignore]'d).", at: "2026-06-04T16:49:55Z")

fact Tag(workitem: "WI-380", name: "typing")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-380", author: "user", content: "From WI-387 delivery + /code-review (3 forward-looking findings for the broader producer rewrite): (S1) Once a concrete carrier WRITES E (List provides Stream[E={}]), a PRIMITIVE Stream op consumed on that carrier with carrier=Some but E omitted from the goal now dispatches NoCandidates (was Unique pre-WI-387). This is by design: the carrier-less effect-row skip in collect_provides_candidates is gated on goal.carrier.is_none() to preserve WI-357 element threading (making carrier=Some match -> the Unique arm re-derives and clobbers the WI-357 re-walk -> ?_ element). BENIGN now (List's Stream ops are body-less specs / List.splitFirst resolves at RUNTIME: eval wi343 + wi362 green), but when WI-380 writes E on producers WITH bodies, re-check the lost static dispatch; the deeper fix is making the Unique arm not clobber the element re-walk. (S2) FIX 2's subtype None-arm REJECTS an OPEN-E provider (fact Stream[T], no E binding -- LogicalStream's shape) against a written Stream[E={}] expectation (provider supplies no E -> reject) instead of absorbing the open row to {}. Conservative-sound; so a carrier kept on bare fact Stream[T] won't satisfy Stream[E={}]. WI-380 should either write E explicitly on each producer or add open-row->{} absorption (WI-307). (E2 altitude) FIX 2 (subtype), FIX 3 (abstract-coverage) and the dispatch None-arm each independently re-derive 'is this provider binding ground/non-discriminating' because bind_spec_params_from_carrier threads only type-param-REF provider bindings into the subst (drops ground rows like E={}); consider threading ground bindings, or a shared provider_binding_for_short helper, when WI-380 touches this.", at: "2026-06-04T18:45:35Z")
